{"language_code":"eng","language_probability":0.9902089834213257,"text":"Elon Musk lost almost $80 billion in a single day, and he didn't buy anything, sell anything, or spend a single cent. Wait, so where did all that money go? It was never sitting in a bank. Most of Elon's fortune is Tesla and SpaceX stock, stacked up like a giant tower. Breaking tonight, after the midterm elections, Tesla stock falls about 11%, and SpaceX drops 8%. When the price drops, the tower shrinks, even though Elon still owns every single share. That's called paper wealth, and it only turns into real money when you sell. Over two days, Bloomberg says his paper fortune fell by about $113 billion, and he's still the richest person on Earth. Elon didn't spend a dollar, and he still lost 80 billion of them. If you own stocks, your money works the same way, and a paper loss only becomes real when you panic and sell.","words":[{"text":"Elon","start":0.1,"end":0.36,"type":"word","logprob":-0.00004541770613286644},{"text":" ","start":0.36,"end":0.42,"type":"spacing","logprob":-0.0000605564855504781},{"text":"Musk","start":0.42,"end":0.72,"type":"word","logprob":-0.0000605564855504781},{"text":" ","start":0.72,"end":0.82,"type":"spacing","logprob":-0.00010311071673640981},{"text":"lost","start":0.82,"end":1.08,"type":"word","logprob":-0.00010311071673640981},{"text":" ","start":1.08,"end":1.18,"type":"spacing","logprob":-2.622600959512056e-6},{"text":"almost","start":1.18,"end":1.48,"type":"word","logprob":-2.622600959512056e-6},{"text":" ","start":1.48,"end":1.66,"type":"spacing","logprob":-0.003246158827096224},{"text":"$80","start":1.66,"end":1.96,"type":"word","logprob":-0.0010824900428640187},{"text":" ","start":1.96,"end":2.18,"type":"spacing","logprob":-4.410734163684538e-6},{"text":"billion","start":2.18,"end":2.54,"type":"word","logprob":-4.410734163684538e-6},{"text":" ","start":2.54,"end":2.6,"type":"spacing","logprob":-0.00015853578224778175},{"text":"in","start":3.12,"end":3.18,"type":